      "decision_by": "Secretary of State (Steve Reed)",
      "decision_status": "Subject to Parliamentary approval; legally confirmed only once a Structural Change Order is made.",
      "shadow_authority_elections": "2027-05",
      "vesting_day": "2028-04-01"
    },
    "name_caveat": "None of the unitary names below are statutory. The six sponsoring councils' business case used North Lancashire / Fylde Coast / South Lancashire / East Lancashire; the county council's post-decision press release used North / West / East / South Lancashire, which confusingly reuses 'West Lancashire' for both a new unitary and a folded-in district. ('Pennine Lancashire' is the name of the rejected 3-unitary model's eastern unit, not a 4-unitary unit.) Preston's leader has said publicly it is 'too early to even know what our new unitary authority's name will be'. Treat all labels as working geographic shorthand only.",
